Teacher Education Learning and Behavior Disorders (LBD) Moderate and Severe Disabilities (MSD) Proficiency Program Teacher Leader Teach KY @ GC Tuition and Financial Aid Majors and Minors Programs of Distinction Christian Scholars Program Fine Arts Health Scholars Independent Honors Oxford Honors Pre-Law Science Honors Provost/Academic Office Registrar: Class Registration/Transcripts Advanced Placement (AP) Credit College Level Examination Program (CLEP) Equivalencies FERPA Final Exam Schedule International Baccalaureate (IB) Credit Resources Academic Calendar Advising and Academic Support Career Preparation Disability Services Ensor LRC (Library) FAQs Transfer Credits Study Abroad Career Preparation “After leaving GC, I obtained my PhD in clinical psychology at Louisiana State University (LSU). I am currently working at a private practice in Louisville, conducting evaluations for children and adolescents suspected of autism spectrum disorders, ADHD, learning disorders, and other behavioral/emotional concerns. I keep in touch with some of the GC psych professors, and they are always willing to answer my questions. I am very appreciative of my time at Georgetown!” BRIAN BELVA ’07 “Georgetown College encouraged me to find ways to combine my education and my passion for community service. An accounting professor connected me with the local Volunteer Income Tax Assistance (VITA) program, where I volunteered during my senior year, and I now work as the Director of the program in Louisville, KY.” BRITTANY SIMS ’15 The Graves Center for Calling and Career 502.863.8082 Email THE GRAVES CENTER FOR CALLING AND CAREER The Graves Center for Calling and Career is your one-stop office for: Assessment of passions, goals, and skills toward career identification Exploration of potential career paths Assistance with job and graduate/professional school applications, including reviewing resumes and letters of interest Preparation for job and graduate/professional school interviews Internship facilitation LOOKING FOR AN ON-CAMPUS JOB? Only current Georgetown College students are eligible to apply for the positions listed below. Click the link to go to ADP, where you will submit your cover letter and resume for the positions that interest you. Please note that some positions are available only to work-study students. Your work-study eligibility should be listed in your Georgetown financial aid offer letter. 91% A breakout number related to Admission Requirements Elsewhere in Admissions & Aid Add Your Heading Text Here Add Your Heading Text Here Add Your Heading Text Here Add Your Heading Text Here TAKE THE NEXT STEP Your future is here—get started fulfilling it! APPLY NOW Schedule a visit Request Information GEORGETOWN STORIES View All Filed Under: Uncategorized Eric Snyder Selected as Fourth Head Men’s Volleyball Coach Posted September 2, 2026 GEORGETOWN, Ky. – Georgetown College Vice President for Athletics Chris Oliver has named Eric Snyder as the Tigers’ fourth head coach of the men’s volleyball program... Filed Under: Uncategorized Dr. Tim Griffith Honored with the Walker Manning Teaching Award Posted August 28, 2026 During our Opening Convocation, held on August 25, 2026, Dr. Tim Griffith was honored with the John Walker Manning Award. This annual award recognizes faculty... Filed Under: Academics New Graduate Program: Clinical Mental Health Counseling Posted July 14, 2026 Georgetown College is proud to announce our first new graduate program outside of teacher education since the 1950s. The Counselor Education program at Georgetown College... Filed Under: Academics , General Presenting the Class of 2026! Posted June 23, 2026 FOUNDED IN 1829, GEORGETOWN COLLEGE ENTERS ITS 197TH YEAR, CELEBRATING 294 UNDERGRADUATE AND GRADUATE DEGREE RECIPIENTS. By Bethany H. Langdon ‘93, Senior Vice President for... Georgetown College 400 East College St Georgetown, KY 40324 Find Us on a Map 502.863.8000 SAFETY: 502.863.1111 Facebook X-twitter Instagram Yout